<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Korea Flour buys 16,900T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Korea Flour buys 16,900T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Flour Milling Corp said on Wednesday it bought 16,900 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp.</p>
<p>An official with Korea Flour said arrival was set to the western port city of Mokpo. Shipment was slated for June 1-30 from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Details of the result were as follows:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	     Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  6,000	 $170.15</p>
<p>(protein min 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  2,500	 $171.25</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	   4,400	 $184.45</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    4,000	 $190.35</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
